<title>FRANCE: Gan, AGF rise on merger hopes.</title>
<headline>Gan, AGF rise on merger hopes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in insurers Gan and AGF rose on Tuesday on merger speculation, particularly on talk of a possible takeover of Gan by AGF, market sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the Axa/UAP phenomenon in the insurance sector which is making AGF move,&quot; said a market operator.</p>
<p>Gan was up four percent at 109.20 francs and Assurances Generales de France rose 4.17 percent to 187.50 at 1110 GMT.</p>
<p>Speculation on various schemes has run in the market, including AGF buying the Athena unit from the Worms group, AGF buying Gan and AGF being bought by a foreign company, Allianz being the most often-cited name.</p>
</text>
